 Os or Ir) concentration before partition]. Another 5-ml portion of supernatant was added to 5 ml of water-saturated octanol, shaken intensively at laboratory temperature for 2 hr and separated carefully. The metal concentration was determined by ICP-MS. The equation log P = log([M]WSO/[M]OSWa) was used, where [M]OSWa stand for the M concentration after the partition and [M]WSO = [M]OSWb - [M]OSWa. The experiment was conducted in triplicate and the results are given as arithmetic mean ± SD."}]}